  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element:the-img-element-12) uses the value of the \"src\" attribute as a criteria to determine what the `img` element represents:\n\n> What an [img](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-img-element) element represents depends on the [src](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-src) attribute and the [alt](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-alt) attribute.\n\n\nHowever, the `src` attribute was made optional, as resolved in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9181. \n\nThe algorithm should probably use the result of the [`selecting an image source`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#selecting-an-image-source).",
